- PTrace
    - PTRACE_TRACEME flag is automatically added by parent
    - Peekdata binding doesn't work, C imports needed
- Process memory
    - only textarea is rwx, other areas might be read only therefore breakpoint insertion is not allowed
      (Including single stepping.)
- Breakpoint insertion
    - Overrides one byte in the current instruction, needs to be replaced with the original data
    - To prevent unexpected behaviour, the PC is set back by one byte to rerun the replaced instruction.
- Printing instructions
    - Instruction length varies
    - Printing &PC print the entire memory data, which may include the next instruction.
    - Technically we can get the offset between two lines of assembly, but that would require objdump
    - Translating bytecode to assembly could solve it.

